+### Compound Durations
+
+`parseCompound` sums several `<number><unit>` pieces, separated by whitespace and/or commas.
+
+```ts
+import { parseCompound } from 'ms';
+
+parseCompound('1h 30m');         // 5400000
+parseCompound('1h, 30m');        // 5400000
+parseCompound('2 days 4 hours'); // 187200000
+```
+
+Unlike `parse`, it never returns `NaN`: invalid input throws a `TypeError`. Every piece must have a unit, so `'1h 30'` is invalid.
+
 ### Enhanced Type Safety
 
 If you want strict type checking for the input value, you can use `parseStrict`.
